From 0e82d465968633f40db0e1230627cbb54c415db4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tryinget <markus@team-wangler.de>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 23:59:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] feat(page): typed page readiness (page.readiness,
 wait.ready)

Waiting for a selector on a page that bounced to a login form, hit an
anti-bot interstitial or rendered a 404 only times out and hides the
cause. This adds a readiness classifier that reports a typed state and
a bounded poll that fails fast with a typed error code.

States: ready, empty, loading, login, challenge, not-found, error.
Every rule is site-independent: browser error URLs, vendor-neutral
challenge markup, generic title/heading wording, visible password
fields (visible UI state, not DOM presence), login-looking routes, and
the caller's own expectations (--selector, --text, --url-prefix,
--empty-text). An explicit empty render is a positive state so callers
can tell "no results" from "blocked".

- src/utils/page-readiness.ts: pure classifier and patterns.
- src/utils/readiness-poll.ts: bounded poll loop (timeout <= 120 s,
  interval >= 50 ms, always one probe, never sleeps past the deadline).
- src/content/page-readiness-probe.ts: DOM snapshot adapter; the
  content script answers PAGE_READINESS and PING.
- Service worker: PAGE_READINESS (one probe) and WAIT_FOR_READY, which
  throws BrowserCommandError page_login / page_challenge /
  page_not_found / page_error / page_timeout unless --accept lists the
  state. A blank tab is loading, a restricted page is error, an
  unreachable content script is loading.
- Host mapping for wait.ready and page.readiness (CLI and socket API
  spellings), CLI help entries and plain-text output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
